ALGORITHM: SPECIAL-MATRIX-MULTIPLICATION(A, B, n)

1. If n = 1
      Return A × B

2. Divide A into:
      A1 and A2

   where

      A = | A1  A2 |
          | A2  A1 |

3. Divide B into:
      B1 and B2

   where

      B = | B1  B2 |
          | B2  B1 |

4. Calculate:
      P = (A1 + A2)(B1 + B2)

5. Calculate:
      Q = (A1 - A2)(B1 - B2)

6. Calculate:
      C = (P + Q) / 2

      D = (P - Q) / 2

7. Form the result:

      Result = | C  D |
               | D  C |

8. Return Result.


TIME COMPLEXITY

T(n) = 2T(n/2) + O(n^2)

Therefore,
T(n) = O(n^2)

